// Native canonical-IPA data manifest for Min Dong / Eastern Min (cdo) — Fuzhou dialect, Sinitic, tonal, ~9M.
// Consumed by foochow.ts. Input = Bàng-uâ-cê (BUC / Foochow Romanized). Converter: [initial] + rime (tight/loose per
// the 韻變 register) + tone → IPA. Missionary convention: ⟨p t k⟩=[pʰ tʰ kʰ], ⟨b d g⟩=[p t k], ⟨c⟩=[t͡s], ⟨ch⟩=[t͡sʰ].
// PHASE 2: the 韻變 (rime alternation) is now MODELLED, not folded — each rime has a TIGHT form (rimes) and, where it
// alternates, a LOOSE form (rimesLoose), selected by the tone register: the LOOSE tones are 陰去/陰入 (acute) + 陽去
// (circumflex) — looseMarks; the tight tones are 陰平/陽平/上聲/陽入. The ⟨io iong iok ioh⟩ family additionally picks
// its medial [y]/[u] by the INITIAL place ([y] after a velar/laryngeal/zero onset, [u] elsewhere) → ioFamily
// (key "rime|medial|register"). Maps derived (reference-parity) from the kaikki BUC↔IPA pairs. Tone sandhi (連讀變調),
// initial assimilation (聲母類化), and the Han front-end remain deferred. See docs/investigations/cdo_native_bringup_investigation.md.
